Trace Daemon Configurations file located under /var/log/nvmesh/trace_daemon and to be named tracedaemon.conf.

TRACE_DAEMON_DBG <\d> - set debug level
TRACE_BUFS_PER_LOG=<\d+> - how many buffers of 4k will be saved to each log file on the disk
TRACE_BUFS_PER_LOG_<channel_name>=<\d+)  - how many buffers of 4k will be saved to each log file on the disk for specifc channel_name
TRACE_MAX_LOGS=<\d+> - how many log files should be saved for this channel - will used with max(set_value, num_of_cpus)
TRACE_MAX_LOGS_<channel_name> - as above but for specific channel
TRACE_LOGS_PATH=<\s+> - path to store the logs into, default is current folder. there will special handling if path is of NFS type

These configurations are only supported when running daemon via run_trace_daemon
NFS_TARGET=<\s+> - Target address, if mentioned the target will be mounted to TRACE_LOGS_PATH and $hostname folder will be created where logs will reside, Example: 10.10.110.2:/var/nfs
NFS_OPTS=<\s+> - opts to be added to mount cmd, for example -o rdma,port=20049
NFS_FALLBACK_LOCAL_STORAGE="Yes", if set and mount cmds fails it will just use the TRACE_LOGS_PATH to store the logs locally
DISABLE_COREDUMP="Yes", if set no coredump for treace daemon will be generated

NFS Server example:
Taken from https://www.howtoforge.com/tutorial/setting-up-an-nfs-server-and-client-on-centos-7/

yum -y install nfs-utils
systemctl enable nfs-server.service
systemctl start nfs-server.service
mkdir /var/nfs
chown nfsnobody:nfsnobody /var/nfs
chmod 755 /var/nfs
vim /etc/exports:
/var/nfs        192.168.0.0/16(rw,sync,no_subtree_check)
exportfs -a

NFS server Tune:
please use this article http://nfs.sourceforge.net/nfs-howto/ar01s05.html
